Paragraph (1) amended by the [https://trello.com/c/qn4kkp63/738-public-safety-and-violent-crime-deterrence-act](https://trello.com/c/qn4kkp63/738-public-safety-and-violent-crime-deterrence-act "smartCard-inline")  to read:
”(1) Authorized Terms. The authorized terms of imprisonment are:
(a) for a Class A felony, no more than 144 hours;
(b) for a Class B felony, no more than 120 hours;
(c) for a Class C felony, no more than 96 hours;
(d)for a Class A misdemeanor, no more than 48 hours;
(e) for a Class B misdemeanor, no more than 36 hours. Such terms shall be administered as provided in part C of this Code.”

Section amended to insert as Paragraph (3), the following:
”(3) Maximum Limits. The aggregate maximum of consecutive sentences to which a defendant may be subject shall not exceed 168 hours.”

