**(1) Authorized Terms.** The authorized terms of imprisonment are:

(a) for a Class A felony, no more than 60 minutes;

(b) for a Class B felony, no more than 50 minutes;

(c) for a Class C felony, no more than 30 minutes;

(d) for a Class A misdemeanor, no more than 25 minutes;

(e) for a Class B misdemeanor, no more than 20 minutes.

Such terms shall be administered as provided in part C of this Code.

‌

**(2) Components of Maximum Term for Indefinite Sentence.** A sentence of imprisonment of more than twenty minutes shall be an indefinite sentence. The maximum term of every indefinite sentence imposed by the court may include a subsequent a probation component. The probation component shall be half of the periods provided in [section 3102](https://trello.com/c/KNmsAAgO/10-3102-incidents-of-probation "‌").

